==English==
[[File:Flower trellis 1.jpg|thumb|A trellis for growing climbing plants]]

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{m|enm|trelis}}, from {{etyl|xno|en}} {{m|fro|treslis}}, from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{m|fro|treille||arbor}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|trichila||arbor", "summer house}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈtɹɛlɪs/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|trellises}}

# An outdoor garden [[frame]] which can be used for partitioning a common area.
# An outdoor garden frame which can be used to grow [[vine]]s or other climbing plants.
# {{lb|en|computing theory}} A kind of [[graph]] used in [[communication theory]] and [[encryption]].

